    "terrainName": "basic-desert",
    "description": "What: the DRAGON breathes fire from its mouth (CE-4634 D-1, docs/designs/fun/DESIGN_Dragon.md DR-4\u2026DR-6). On basic-desert a 'Dragon' (TKB 411) stands at (300, 300) facing east with a 'Pillion' rifleman aboard its firing seat; it breathes at (325, 300) (FireAtPoint, mount 0). 'Field Man 1' (322, 300) and 'Field Man 2' (330, 302) stand in the flame; 'Bystander' (325, 280) stands 20 m south, out of it. A hostile flamethrower man, 'Dragon Hunter' at (300, 285), flames the dragon's flank. Judge: the dragon spends its fire; both field men burn and Field Man 1 dies; the bystander is never hurt; the pillion is never hurt by his own dragon; the hunter spends fuel and the dragon is never hurt by his flame (a dragon is fireproof)."
  },
